IMPORT prelude

-- Mississippi Code of 1972, s 43-17-5: Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF). The most a family's budget may
-- receive (subs. (1)); the family cap (subs. (1)); who must be denied (subs. (3)); the duty to report a child's absence
-- (subs. (3)(h)); school attendance and its sanctions (subs. (4)); vaccination and its sanction (subs. (5)); work activity,
-- its exemptions, hours, the job search workshop and the work sanctions (subs. (6)).
--
-- SEAT: the parent or caretaker relative who applies for, or receives, TANF: "How much TANF can my family get? Will we be
-- denied? Must I work, and for how many hours? What happens if I miss a requirement?" Duties of the Department of Human
-- Services are encoded for what they mean to that person.
--
-- Source and edition. The official Code (LexisNexis) was not used: see ../../SOURCE-LICENSE.md. The text of s 43-17-5 comes
-- from the Legislature's House Bill 121 of the 2026 Regular Session, as introduced, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ms-2026-hb0121-introduced-43-17-5.txt. The bill proposed to double the amounts in
-- subsection (1) and died in committee on 3 February 2026. Its reprint shows the section in force with the proposal marked:
-- the struck text ([[deleted: ...]]) is the law; the underlined text ([[inserted: ...]]) is the proposal that failed. The
-- encoding uses the struck amounts ($200, $36, $24). NOTES.md says how far the reprint can be trusted as current.
--
-- The Department's regulations (the standard of need, income counting, the payment within the maximums) are not deposited;
-- the family's grant before sanctions is an input where a question needs it.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: subsections (2), (7) to (14) (benefit delivery, child care, transportation, Medicaid, contracts, reports);
-- the drug testing requirement of s 43-17-6 (asked as a fact); the fair hearing procedure.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mississippi TANF -- s 43-17-5`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

§§ `s 43-17-5(1) -- the most my family can get`

-- "The first family member in the dependent child's budget may receive an amount not to exceed * * * [[deleted: Two
-- Hundred Dollars ($200.00)]] per month; the second family member ... * * * [[deleted: Thirty-six Dollars ($36.00)]] per
-- month; and each additional family member ... * * * [[deleted: Twenty-four Dollars ($24.00)]] per month. The maximum for
-- any individual family member ... may be exceeded for foster or medical care or in cases of children with an intellectual
-- disability or a physical disability."
GIVEN `members in the dependent child's budget` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the budget may receive` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `members in the dependent child's budget` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0
        IF `members in the dependent child's budget` EQUALS 1 THEN 200
        OTHERWISE 200 PLUS 36 PLUS 24 TIMES (`members in the dependent child's budget` MINUS 2)

@export What is the most TANF my family's budget may receive each month (s 43-17-5(1))? The amount itself is set by the county department within these limits.
GIVEN `family members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many family members are in the dependent child's TANF budget
      `foster, medical or disability case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member's limit is exceeded for foster care, medical care, or a child with an intellectual or physical disability (then the limits below do not cap that member)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most TANF my family can get` MEANS
    IF `foster, medical or disability case` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (`the most the budget may receive` `family members`)

-- "TANF benefits granted shall be specifically limited only (a) to children existing or conceived at the time the caretaker
-- relative initially applies and qualifies for such assistance, unless this limitation is specifically waived by the
-- department, or (b) to a child born following a twelve-consecutive-month period of discontinued benefits".
@export Can TANF be granted for this child (the family cap in s 43-17-5(1))?
GIVEN `existing or conceived at first application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was born, or already conceived, when you first applied and qualified for TANF
      `born after a 12-month break` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was born after your TANF had been stopped for twelve months in a row
      `the department waived the limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Department of Human Services has waived the limitation for this child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can TANF be granted for this child` IF
        `existing or conceived at first application`
    OR  `born after a 12-month break`
    OR  `the department waived the limit`

§§ `s 43-17-5(3) -- will my family be denied`

-- "The Department of Human Services shall deny TANF benefits to the following categories of individuals, except for
-- individuals and families specifically exempt or excluded for good cause as allowed by federal statute or regulation".
-- The categories a family can state are below; (k) fleeing felons, (l) unqualified aliens, (m) residence fraud convictions,
-- (n) SSI recipients and (o) drug testing noncompliance are grouped as one fact per person.
DECLARE `TANF denial` IS ONE OF
    `not denied under s 43-17-5(3) on the facts given`
    `denied: no minor child resides with the custodial parent or other adult caretaker relative (s 43-17-5(3)(a))`
    `denied: an adult has received TANF for 60 months (s 43-17-5(3)(b))`
    `denied: the family has not assigned its support rights to the state (s 43-17-5(3)(c))`
    `denied: the family has not cooperated in establishing paternity or obtaining child support (s 43-17-5(3)(d))`
    `denied: a parent or caretaker relative has not engaged in an allowable work activity once found ready to work or after 24 months of TANF (s 43-17-5(3)(j))`
    `denied for that individual: a category in s 43-17-5(3)(e) to (i) or (k) to (o) applies`

@export Will my family be denied TANF under s 43-17-5(3)?
GIVEN `minor child at home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a child under 18 lives with you as the custodial parent or adult caretaker relative
      `months of TANF` IS A NUMBER @desc The most months any adult in your family has received TANF since the Mississippi TANF program began (consecutive or not)
      `support assigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family has assigned to the state its rights to child or spousal support, as the law requires
      `cooperating on support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are cooperating in establishing paternity and obtaining child support (answer TRUE if you have good cause not to)
      `work required now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Department has found you ready to work, or you have received TANF for 24 months or more
      `in work activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are engaged in an allowable work activity (or exempt from it)
      `individual category applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of these applies to a member: a teen parent not in school or not living with an adult; a child away from home for more than 30 days; not following the Employability Development Plan; fleeing prosecution; not a qualified alien; a residence fraud conviction in the last 10 years; receiving SSI; not complying with the drug testing rules
      `exempt for good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family or the individual is specifically exempt or excluded for good cause as federal law allows
GIVETH A `TANF denial`
`Will my family be denied TANF` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `exempt for good cause` THEN `not denied under s 43-17-5(3) on the facts given`
        IF (NOT `minor child at home`) THEN `denied: no minor child resides with the custodial parent or other adult caretaker relative (s 43-17-5(3)(a))`
        IF `months of TANF` AT LEAST 60 THEN `denied: an adult has received TANF for 60 months (s 43-17-5(3)(b))`
        IF (NOT `support assigned`) THEN `denied: the family has not assigned its support rights to the state (s 43-17-5(3)(c))`
        IF (NOT `cooperating on support`) THEN `denied: the family has not cooperated in establishing paternity or obtaining child support (s 43-17-5(3)(d))`
        IF `work required now` AND (NOT `in work activity`) THEN `denied: a parent or caretaker relative has not engaged in an allowable work activity once found ready to work or after 24 months of TANF (s 43-17-5(3)(j))`
        IF `individual category applies` THEN `denied for that individual: a category in s 43-17-5(3)(e) to (i) or (k) to (o) applies`
        OTHERWISE `not denied under s 43-17-5(3) on the facts given`

§§ `s 43-17-5(6) -- work activity`

-- (6)(b): "An adult may be exempt from the mandatory work activity requirement for the following reasons: (i) Incapacity;
-- (ii) Temporary illness or injury, verified by physician's certificate; (iii) ... third trimester of pregnancy, and there
-- are complications verified ...; (iv) Caretaker of a child under twelve (12) months, for not more than twelve (12) months of
-- the sixty-month maximum benefit period; (v) Caretaker of an ill or incapacitated person ...; (vi) Age, if over sixty (60)
-- or under eighteen (18) years of age; (vii) Receiving treatment for substance abuse, if ... in compliance ...; (viii) In a
-- two-parent family, the caretaker of a severely disabled child ...; or (ix) History of having been a victim of domestic
-- violence ... not to exceed a total of twelve (12) months".
@export Am I exempt from the TANF work activity requirement (s 43-17-5(6)(b))?
GIVEN `incapacity, illness or complicated late pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incapacitated, temporarily ill or injured (with a physician's certificate), or in the third trimester of pregnancy with certified complications
      `caring for a baby under 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you care for a child under 12 months old
      `months already exempt for a baby` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you have already been exempt for caring for a child under 12 months
      `caring for an ill person or disabled child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you care for an ill or incapacitated person (physician-certified), or, in a two-parent family, a severely disabled child
      `age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `in substance abuse treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving substance abuse treatment and complying with the treatment plan
      `domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a substantiated history of domestic violence (police or court records) and are at risk of more
      `months already exempt for domestic violence` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you have already been exempt for domestic violence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I exempt from work activity` IF
        `incapacity, illness or complicated late pregnancy`
    OR  (`caring for a baby under 12 months` AND `months already exempt for a baby` LESS THAN 12)
    OR  `caring for an ill person or disabled child`
    OR  `age` GREATER THAN 60
    OR  `age` LESS THAN 18
    OR  `in substance abuse treatment`
    OR  (`domestic violence` AND `months already exempt for domestic violence` LESS THAN 12)

-- (6)(c): "not fewer than twenty (20) hours per week (thirty-five (35) hours per week for two-parent families)".
@export How many hours a week of work activity must I do at least (s 43-17-5(6)(c))?
GIVEN `two-parent family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether yours is a two-parent family
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours of work activity` MEANS IF `two-parent family` THEN 35 ELSE 20

-- (6)(e): "(i) For the first violation, the department shall terminate the TANF assistance otherwise payable to the family
-- for a two-month period or until the person has complied ..., whichever is longer; (ii) ... second violation ... six-month
-- period ...; (iii) ... third violation ... twelve-month period ...; (iv) For the fourth violation, the person shall be
-- permanently disqualified."
DECLARE `Work sanction` IS ONE OF
    `family TANF terminated for at least` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER
    `permanently disqualified (s 43-17-5(6)(e)(iv))`

@export If I refuse required work activity, for how long is my family's TANF terminated (s 43-17-5(6)(e))? It lasts longer if I have still not complied.
GIVEN `violation number` IS A NUMBER @desc Which violation this is: 1 for the first, 2 for the second, and so on
GIVETH A `Work sanction`
`What is the work sanction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `violation number` AT MOST 1 THEN `family TANF terminated for at least` 2
        IF `violation number` EQUALS 2 THEN `family TANF terminated for at least` 6
        IF `violation number` EQUALS 3 THEN `family TANF terminated for at least` 12
        OTHERWISE `permanently disqualified (s 43-17-5(6)(e)(iv))`

§§ `s 43-17-5(4), (5) -- school attendance and vaccination sanctions (only once a sanction is imposed)`

-- (4)(f): "the department shall discontinue or deny TANF benefits to the child thirteen (13) years old, or older" who
-- without good cause failed the attendance requirement, and "shall discontinue or deny twenty-five percent (25%) of the
-- family grant when a child six (6) through twelve (12) years of age" failed it; "Both the child and family sanction may
-- apply". (5): if the parents "fail to comply after thirty (30) days' notice, the department shall sanction the family's
-- TANF benefits by twenty-five percent (25%)". The text does not say how two 25% sanctions combine; each is taken of the
-- family grant before sanctions (NOTES.md finding 3). The teenager's share of the grant is an input.
GIVEN `family grant before sanctions` IS A NUMBER
      `share of a sanctioned teenager aged 13 or over` IS A NUMBER
      `a child aged 6 to 12 failed attendance without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `vaccinations not done after 30 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the grant after the subsection (4) and (5) sanctions` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0
        (sum (LIST
            `family grant before sanctions`,
            0 MINUS `share of a sanctioned teenager aged 13 or over`,
            IF `a child aged 6 to 12 failed attendance without good cause` THEN 0 MINUS (25% TIMES `family grant before sanctions`) ELSE 0,
            IF `vaccinations not done after 30 days' notice` THEN 0 MINUS (25% TIMES `family grant before sanctions`) ELSE 0))

@export How much TANF will my family get after a school attendance or vaccination sanction (s 43-17-5(4)(f), (5))?
GIVEN `grant` IS A NUMBER @desc Your family's monthly TANF grant before any sanction, in US dollars
      `teenager's share` IS A NUMBER @desc If a child aged 13 or over has been sanctioned for school attendance: the part of the grant for that child, in US dollars; else 0
      `younger child missed school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a child aged 6 to 12 has failed the monthly attendance requirement without good cause
      `vaccinations missing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your children's required vaccinations were still not done 30 days after the Department's notice, without good cause
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much TANF after school or vaccination sanctions` MEANS
    `the grant after the subsection (4) and (5) sanctions` `grant` `teenager's share` `younger child missed school` `vaccinations missing`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `TANF party` IS ONE OF `the parent or caretaker relative`, `the TANF recipient`, `the Department of Human Services`
DECLARE `TANF act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the department of the child's absence`
    `participate in a job search skills training workshop or job readiness program`
    `have the children receive the required vaccinations`
    `sanction the family's TANF benefits by 25%`

-- (3)(h): a parent or caretaker relative "who fails to notify the department of the absence of the minor child from the
-- home for the thirty-day period specified in paragraph (g), by the end of the five-day period that begins with the date
-- that it becomes clear to the individual that the minor child will be absent for the thirty-day period" is denied TANF.
-- The five-day period begins on that date, so it is day 0 and the period ends at the end of day 4.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TANF party` `TANF act`
`s 43-17-5(3)(h) -- notify the department of a child's 30-day absence within the five-day period` MEANS
    PARTY  `the parent or caretaker relative`
    MUST   `notify the department of the child's absence`
    WITHIN 4
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the parent or caretaker relative` BECAUSE "the child's 30-day absence not notified within the five-day period; TANF is denied to that individual (s 43-17-5(3)(h))"

-- (6)(b): "Within sixty (60) days after the initial application for TANF benefits, the TANF recipient must participate in a
-- job search skills training workshop or a job readiness program". Counted from the application (day 0).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TANF party` `TANF act`
`s 43-17-5(6)(b) -- the job search skills workshop within 60 days of applying` MEANS
    PARTY  `the TANF recipient`
    MUST   `participate in a job search skills training workshop or job readiness program`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the TANF recipient` BECAUSE "no job search skills training workshop or job readiness program within 60 days after the initial application (s 43-17-5(6)(b))"

-- (5): "If the parents without good cause do not have their dependent children receive the vaccinations ... and they fail
-- to comply after thirty (30) days' notice, the department shall sanction the family's TANF benefits by twenty-five percent
-- (25%)". Counted from the notice (day 0): comply within 30 days; failing that, the Department must sanction ("shall";
-- "for the next payment month", which has no fixed day here, so no deadline is set).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `TANF party` `TANF act`
`s 43-17-5(5) -- vaccinations within 30 days of notice, or a 25% sanction` MEANS
    PARTY  `the parent or caretaker relative`
    MUST   `have the children receive the required vaccinations`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Department of Human Services`
        MUST  `sanction the family's TANF benefits by 25%`
